{"id":"4d824a15-131d-4d1f-829e-a2823e6ccf9f","kind":"note","ref":{"span":"672d52b620a73696","key":"bablr1","file":"packages/editor/shell/reset.ts","baseline":{"blob":"7f6455a144fb13a84ad31feb047a10cd03d20ba5","start":3543,"end":3796},"shape":{"type":"ExportDeclaration","atoms":["export","function","resetAsked","(",")",":","\"","keep-sign-in","\"","|","\"","all","\"","|","\"","wait","\"","|","undefined","{","const","asked","=","new","URLSearchParams","(","location",".","search",")",".","get","(","\"","reset","\"",")",";","return","asked","===","null","?","undefined",":","asked","===","\"","all","\"","||","asked","===","\"","wait","\"","?","asked",":","\"","keep-sign-in","\"",";","}"]},"context":{"before":"468531432cb220fa","after":"985338008d6315e3"}},"payload":{"text":"What the address asks: a reset keeping the sign-in, one signing out too, to wait out another tab's, or none.","wrote":["Brian Jenkins"]},"author":"local","createdAt":"2026-11-22T17:40:35.792Z","updatedAt":"2026-11-22T17:40:35.792Z"}
{"id":"5436339a-838f-49f7-a588-2dac206a3a00","kind":"note","ref":{"span":"0b63740c2729e487","key":"bablr1","file":"packages/editor/shell/reset.ts","baseline":{"blob":"fbb0f9f12962670a7cfa97d38cc6a09b9309a1e3","start":0,"end":52},"shape":{"type":"ImportDeclaration","atoms":["import","{","logger","}","from","\"","@brianjenkins94/util/logger","\""]},"context":{"after":"e76930f4f0b18f50"}},"payload":{"text":"Resetting the editor: everything this browser keeps for it, gone, so the next load is a first one — the workspace and\nits git, VS Code's own state, BABLR's parses, silo's local records, the shell's settings — and its service worker\nunregistered. The sign-in stays, unless asked to go too (`?reset=all`).\n\nIt runs from the address (`?reset`), first thing (main.tsx), before the service worker or the workbench start: nothing\nin this tab holds a database open then, and an editor too broken to open still resets. The shell's Reset button\nconfirms, then goes there. Only the editor's stores, named: on GitHub Pages it shares its origin with other sites.\n\nThe editor's other tabs hold the same databases open, and a database can't be deleted while one does: the reset tells\nthem (a BroadcastChannel), and each lets go — it goes to `?reset=wait`, which opens nothing — and comes back once the\nreset is done.\n\nAn instance (shared/instance.ts) resets only itself, and leaves the service worker, which serves everyone; resetting the\nreal editor takes its instances with it.","wrote":["Brian Jenkins"]},"author":"local","createdAt":"2026-11-22T17:40:46.697Z","updatedAt":"2026-11-22T17:40:46.697Z"}
{"id":"5db419c3-ced1-4d8f-b596-4e469127e107","kind":"note","ref":{"span":"b41af9d2a0f5aeb2","key":"bablr1","file":"packages/editor/shell/reset.ts","baseline":{"blob":"910130db0465ce2f62d23b9feadc7a045bf89037","start":1969,"end":2053},"shape":{"type":"VariableDeclaration","atoms":["const","CHANNEL","=","instance","===","undefined","?","\"","editor.reset","\"",":","`","editor.reset.","${","instance","}","","`"]},"context":{"before":"670dddc43365cee3","after":"4d9c8aefec3c43d5"}},"payload":{"text":"Where a reset tells the editor's other tabs it's begun and it's done; and the mark it's going on, for a tab that\nopens in the middle of it.","wrote":["Brian Jenkins"]},"author":"local","createdAt":"2026-11-22T17:40:40.033Z","updatedAt":"2026-11-22T17:40:40.033Z"}
